# ---------------------------------------------------------------- vendored
# Every cloned or downloaded repository lands here and is never committed.
# Hard rule 3: anything added under third_party/ must ALSO be listed in
# git.ignoredRepositories in .vscode/settings.json — each clone carries its own
# .git and otherwise shows up in Source Control as noise.
# Hard rule 5: local reference cores (sega-model1-mister, NMK16, ...) are copied
# in here rather than read in place. Same treatment.
/third_party/

# The MiSTer sys/ framework, placed by tools/bootstrap.sh from the vendored
# template. Upstream code, so it follows the same rule as third_party/ rather
# than being committed — most cores commit a copy, but then there are two rules
# for vendored code instead of one.
/sys/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ builds
# Hard rule 10: everything generated lives under build/. The entries below the
# first are for artefacts Quartus and Verilator place elsewhere when a setting
# is missed — kept so a stray one cannot be committed.
# Hard rule 2. Anchored with a leading slash where the top-level directory is
# meant, so that /build/ is not silently satisfied by a nested /quartus/build/.
/build/
/quartus/build/
# releases/ IS committed — it is the distributable, not a build artefact.
# One dated .rbf plus the primary MRAs, in the layout MiSTer expects. Build
# intermediates still live under build/ (rule 10); this is what a tester
# downloads. Old .rbf files are removed rather than accumulated, so the repo
# does not grow a few megabytes per build.
# Generated MRAs live under build/ like everything else generated; the
# published copies are in releases/.
/mra/

!/releases/
# No trailing slash. `make quartus` makes these SYMLINKS into build/ (rule 10),
# and a directory-only pattern does not match a symlink — `db/` left both of
# them untracked-but-not-ignored, one `git add -A` away from being committed.
db
incremental_db
output_files/
greybox_tmp/
simulation/
timing/
.qsys_edit/
qdb/
*.qws
*.rpt
# Quartus drops these in the project root regardless of
# PROJECT_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY — there is no assignment that moves them, so rule 10
# is enforced here instead.
/c5_pin_model_dump.txt
/jtag.cdf
*.summary
*.smsg
*.pin
*.done
*.jdi
*.sld
*.qar
*.qarlog
*.sopcinfo
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# Bitstreams and programming files.
*.sof
*.pof
*.rbf
# ...except the published ones. A blanket *.rbf keeps build output out, and it
# silently swallowed `git add releases/` too — the release bitstream was
# skipped without a word while the old one had just been removed, leaving
# upstream with no core at all. An ignore rule that is right for build/ is not
# automatically right for the one directory whose entire purpose is to carry
# a bitstream.
!/releases/*.rbf
*.jic
*.map
*.fit
*.sta
*.asm

# --------------------------------------------------------------- verilator
# Not obj_<prefix>*/ — a narrower pattern stops covering new harnesses the
# moment one is named differently, and that has already let a build tree
# through in a sibling repository.
obj_dir/
/obj_*/
/sim/**/obj_*/
*.vcd
*.fst
*.fst.hier
*.wlf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- yosys
*.json.yosys
/yosys.log
# abc writes its command history into the working directory on every area run,
# which for this Makefile is the repository root.
/abc.history
*.blif
*.edif

# --------------------------------------------------------------- toolchain
/tools/**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Quartus installer: BOTH the downloaded archive and the unpacked tree. Several
# GB each, and Altera-licensed — redistributing it is not permitted, so neither
# may ever be committed. No trailing slash on the directory rule: a directory-
# only pattern cannot match a path that does not exist yet, and an installer
# script that checks the path is ignored BEFORE creating it would fire on every
# clean run.
/tools/quartus-unpack
/tools/*.tar
/tools/*.tar.*
/tools/Quartus*
/tools/QuartusLiteSetup*
/tools/*.qdz
# Chrome writes "Unconfirmed NNNNN.crdownload" — with a space — which no *.tar
# pattern would ever catch.
*.crdownload
*.part
*.download
*.partial

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- roms
# Hard rule 2: never commit ROM images or anything derived from them, including
# extracted tables baked into source. Load via the MRA path at runtime.
/roms/
/rom/
/build/rom/
*.zip
*.7z
*.hex

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ editor
# Shared project settings are committed; everything else under .vscode/ is not.
# The directory itself must not be excluded — git will not re-include a file
# underneath an excluded directory, so this has to be `.vscode/*`.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# fx68k loads these with $readmemb at runtime, relative to the working
# directory, so bootstrap symlinks them into the repo root. Upstream files.
/microrom.mem
/nanorom.mem

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- local
# Local working instructions, kept on disk but not published.
/CLAUDE.md
